// TRACKERS

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_RESET
LANG_ENGLISH        "RESET"

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_RESET_DESC
LANG_ENGLISH        "The game constantly tracks every active element on the map (zombies, items, doors) and adds them to an internal memory counter 20 times per second. If you survive long enough, this counter reaches its mathematical limit and overflows, causing the game to force a restart back to Round 1 instead of crashing."

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_SCRIPT_USAGE
LANG_ENGLISH        "GSC USAGE"

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_SCRIPT_USAGE_DESC
LANG_ENGLISH        "These appear when the game creates invisible threads to execute tasks (like using the mystery box) and forgets to close them when finished. These inactive threads accumulate in the background until the virtual machine crashes."

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_ENTITY_USAGE
LANG_ENGLISH        "GSPAWN"

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_ENTITY_USAGE_DESC
LANG_ENGLISH        "This occurs when the maximum limit of elements or objects that can exist simultaneously in the game is exceeded. It frequently happens when the game incorrectly registers and deletes zombies before they physically appear."

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_ANIM_INFO
LANG_ENGLISH        "ANIMATION ERROR"

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_ANIM_INFO_DESC
LANG_ENGLISH        "This is caused by a defect in the function responsible for clearing animations, which is especially noticeable with the robots on Origins. The command that should free up space does exactly the opposite, saturating the memory."

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_MEM_USAGE
LANG_ENGLISH        "HUNK ERROR"

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_MEM_USAGE_DESC
LANG_ENGLISH        "The system runs out of memory by accumulating routine actions like swapping weapons or knifing. The game allocates memory space to process these actions but never frees it."

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_STRING_USAGE
LANG_ENGLISH        "MEMORY TREE ERROR"

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_STRING_USAGE_DESC
LANG_ENGLISH        "This happens when elements, such as zombies, are incorrectly deleted from the map, leaving residual data behind. When the memory structure storing this information becomes saturated, the game crashes."

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_VIEW_ANGLES
LANG_ENGLISH        "ROTATION ANGLE ROUNDING"

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_VIEW_ANGLES_DESC
LANG_ENGLISH        "Continuously turning the camera in the same direction causes the game's rotation memory to lose precision, making your aim feel laggy and unresponsive (Aim Lag). If the rotation counter reaches its maximum limit (32,768 full rotations), your camera permanently locks and cannot move left or right anymore (Aim Lock)."

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_SOUNDDONE_REFCOUNT
LANG_ENGLISH        "SOUND FREEZE"

REFERENCE           XOIA_MENU_TRACKER_SOUNDDONE_REFCOUNT_DESC
LANG_ENGLISH        "The game freezes simply from killing too many zombies exactly when they emit a sound. The system is unable to discard that audio effect file and eventually crashes after accumulating thousands of them."

